# Environment Configuration
# Add optional environment variables here

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GITHUB_TOKEN (optional, server-side only)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Used ONLY by server processes to query the official GitHub GraphQL
# contributionCalendar API for the portfolio heatmap:
#   - Local dev / preview: read by vite.config.ts middleware via process.env.
#     Set it in your shell before `npm run dev`, e.g.
#       Windows PowerShell:  $env:GITHUB_TOKEN = "ghp_xxx"
#       bash/zsh:            export GITHUB_TOKEN=ghp_xxx
#   - Production (Firebase Hosting): stored in Google Secret Manager and
#     injected into the Cloud Function at runtime. Set it with:
#       firebase functions:secrets:set GITHUB_TOKEN
#
# SECURITY RULES — never break these:
#   - NEVER name this variable VITE_GITHUB_TOKEN (any VITE_ prefix is baked
#     into the browser bundle and becomes public).
#   - NEVER commit a real token to this repo or paste it into client code.
#   - Scope the token minimally: classic PAT with `read:user` is sufficient.
#
# The site works WITHOUT a token too: the server falls back to the public
# GitHub contribution stream (still genuine data, no mock values).
# GITHUB_TOKEN=
